\\  & =\\alpha (x{e}^{-6x})^{′}+\\beta ({e}^{x})^{′} \\\\  & =\\alpha ({e}^{-6x}-6x{e}^{-6x})+\\beta {e}^{x} \\\\  & =\\alpha (1-6x){e}^{-6x}+\\beta {e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha $ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute ${y}_{p}$ and ${y}_{p}^{′}$ into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\alpha (1-6x){e}^{-6x}+\\beta {e}^{x})+6(\\alpha x{e}^{-6x}+\\beta {e}^{x}) & =30{e}^{-6x}+4{e}^{x} \\\\ (1-6x+6x)\\alpha {e}^{-6x}+(\\beta +6\\beta ){e}^{x} & =30{e}^{-6x}+4{e}^{x} \\\\ \\alpha {e}^{-6x}+7\\beta {e}^{x} & =30{e}^{-6x}+4{e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating coefficients of ${e}^{-6x}$ and ${e}^{x}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\alpha =30\\,\\text{and}\\,7\\beta =4,\n$$\n\nso, we have\n\n$$\n\\alpha =30\\,\\text{and}\\,\\beta =\\frac{4}{7}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=30x{e}^{-6x}+\\frac{4}{7}{e}^{x}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039029/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e201f73a2dcba8817f27f103d4ea9dbb053badeeb1ccdea5bbebfb7a0ae388b"} {"question" "q-332853" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039029/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3608d4e1729d52dbbd5e37178cdaa0e8914aebbc7a9b4520adf64c212f158fea"} {"question" "q-332853" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039029/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e201f73a2dcba8817f27f103d4ea9dbb053badeeb1ccdea5bbebfb7a0ae388b"} {"question" "q-332853" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "30xe^{-6x}+\\frac{4}{7}e^x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/C