n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}^{′} & =(\\alpha x{e}^{-2x})^{′} \\\\  & =\\alpha (x{e}^{-2x})^{′} \\\\  & =\\alpha ({e}^{-2x}-2x{e}^{-2x}) \\\\  & =\\alpha (1-2x){e}^{-2x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the value of $\\alpha ,$ we substitute ${y}_{p}$ and ${y}_{p}^{′}$ into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\alpha (1-2x){e}^{-2x})+2\\alpha x{e}^{-2x} & =6{e}^{-2x} \\\\ (1-2x+2x)\\alpha {e}^{-2x} & =6{e}^{-2x} \\\\ \\alpha {e}^{-2x} & =6{e}^{-2x} \\\\ \\alpha  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=6x{e}^{-2x}.\n$$\n\nNow, since the general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nthe general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-2x}+6x{e}^{-2x}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039029/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e201f73a2dcba8817f27f103d4ea9dbb053badeeb1ccdea5bbebfb7a0ae388b"} {"question" "q-332899" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039029/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3608d4e1729d52dbbd5e37178cdaa0e8914aebbc7a9b4520adf64c212f158fea"} {"question" "q-332899" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039029/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e201f73a2dcba8817f27f103d4ea9dbb053badeeb1ccdea5bbebfb7a0ae388b"} {"question" "q-332899" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "Ae^{-2x}+6xe^{-2x}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039029/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e201f73a2dcba8817f27f103d4ea9dbb053b